          "end_line": 631,
          "quote": "Live domain artifacts, once published as live\nconstitutional surfaces, are immutable in place;",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FLive%20surface%20immutability",
          "start_line": 621
        }
      ],
      "key": "live_constitutional_history",
      "statement": "Live surfaces are versioned constitutional history, not scratch space. Wrong live artifacts are superseded by a new version or withdrawn/deleted from the live surface, never silently mutated in place. Superseded transitional paths, migration scaffolds and fallbacks retire and gain no permanent authority. History remains in version control, operational events where present and superseded artifacts. Compatibility shims need not ship forever.",
      "uncertainty": "The §7 retention relation is referenced but not supplied."
