      "applies_to_keys": ["outcome_work_wave"],
      "conditions": ["A selected outcome instance is being progressed or has been accepted."],
      "exceptions": ["Acceptance exhausts only the bound instance and interval, not enduring guarantees, recurring obligations or a broader family.", "An assurance capability expressly defined as product behaviour may count as product progress; output/evidence roles of the same artifact must be declared separately."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 722,
          "quote": "The exact bound outcome instance stops selecting later product-progress\nwork when the owning authority accepts it;",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F3.%20Outcome%20conservation",
          "start_line": 700
        }
      ],
      "key": "outcome_progress_and_acceptance_interval",
      "statement": "Progress and supported-path promotion are evaluated against the same selected outcome; only accepted material advance projects product progress. After acceptance, witnesses remain preservation/regression evidence; further work is preservation, a bounded prerequisite for another admitted outcome, or a lawfully repriced change, never additional progress on the accepted instance. Choosing another already-defined unresolved outcome is goals/work sequencing; changing meaning/scope or adding an outcome requires Product re-entry. Completed matrices, ledgers, inventories, design artifacts, suites or other evidence cannot select, enlarge or replace the outcome; even product assurance evidence does not author the claim.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["outcome_work_wave"],
      "conditions": ["Material realisation growth within a product-outcome-bearing wave."],
      "exceptions": ["Independent parallel work may proceed under its own admitted basis without counting as the governed outcome's progress.", "A regression/gap promotion block can end through repair, repricing or owning-authority acceptance."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 765,
          "quote": "Ended authority cannot be renewed by repair,\ncontinuation, evidence, active ticket or run state, or prior admission;",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F3.%20Outcome%20conservation",
          "start_line": 748
        }
      ],
      "key": "bounded_growth_authority",
      "statement": "Growth requires selected unresolved outcome, admitted named bounded prerequisite, or admitted named bounded experiment whose observation discriminates a stated decision for it. Prerequisites/experiments authorise only their provisional bounds: no enlarged outcome, downstream authority, promotion, closure or waiver of applicable design/safety/authority/release law. Admission/renewal belongs to wave owner or bounded proxy and is durably recorded in goals/tickets with bounds and exhaustion/falsification conditions. Ticket/contract drafting or validation, active status and prior admission create/extend/renew nothing. Acceptance, prerequisite discharge, experiment observation/decision resolution, admitted terminal condition, rejection, withdrawal, supersession, repricing-away or falsification ends the basis. More material work needs new admission. Retention grants no growth; consumer-owned salvage carries only explicitly re-adopted semantics, not enclosing authority, dependencies, completion or work-selection power. Regression/unresolved gaps block only affected-path promotion. Outcome success is necessary delivery evidence, not complete Product/release closure.",
      "uncertainty": ""
